{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Vibe Coding for Network Security.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Vibe Coding for Network Security.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"vibe coding for network security vibe coding for network security","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Vibe Coding for Network Security.md","fileName":"Vibe Coding for Network Security.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Vibe Coding for Network Security","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 18:30\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[AI-Assisted Network Security]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI-Assisted Network Security","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Vibe Coding for Network Security.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Vibe Coding for Network Security.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"vibe coding for network security vibe coding for network security","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Vibe Coding for Network Security.md","fileName":"Vibe Coding for Network Security.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Vibe Coding for Network Security","heading":"Vibe Coding for Network Security","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Vibe coding for network security develops scripts through an ongoing natural-language conversation with a coding assistant. A practitioner describes the incident or detection goal, reviews the proposed architecture and code, and refines requirements across several rapid iterations.\n\nThe method emphasizes speed and domain expertise over a complete formal specification at the outset. That makes it useful for prototypes, but security requirements cannot remain implicit. Tests, least privilege, supported incident types, evidence handling, and approval rules must become explicit before the prototype can enter an operational workflow.","tags":["baby"],"lin